{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "U1: Convert Add/Update functions to SetXXX with override behavior; for slices like AnchorPeers, implement logic to avoid duplicates when setting by checking existence and replacing or appending appropriately. Rename UpdateXXX to SetXXX for consistency. Update all internal callers and examples.",
    "U2: Rename Base() to OriginalConfig() and Updated() to UpdatedConfig() for clarity. Update all references and GoDoc.",
    "U3: Introduce intermediary wrapper types (e.g., Application, Organization) within configtx package to allow chaining API calls. Each wrapper will hold a reference to the underlying ConfigGroup and provide appropriate getters/setters. Design decision: use pointer receivers and return new wrapper instances to maintain immutability pattern.",
    "U4: Create new package 'configtx/orderer' and move orderer-related types (Kafka, EtcdRaft, BatchSize, ConsensusState) there. Keep all functions in original package unless moving them is deemed necessary for consistency. Update import paths and ensure backward compatibility via type aliases if needed.",
    "U5: Create new package 'configtx/membership' and move MSP-related types (SigningIdentityInfo, OUIdentifier, CryptoConfig, NodeOUs) there. Follow same approach as U4 for functions and aliases.",
    "U6: Modify removal functions to not return an error when the value does not exist. Remove the error return from the function signature where safe, and update callers accordingly. Update GoDoc to document this behavior.",
    "U7: Overhaul GoDoc: remove listed unnecessary example functions, rename remaining examples to descriptive names (e.g., Example_systemChannel → Example_textExample), split into smaller focused examples (e.g., Example_ACLs, Example_policyRetrieval, Example_ordererUpdate, Example_membership), remove Output validation comments, and reformat code blocks to avoid horizontal scrolling by introducing line breaks.",
    "U8: Build a CLI tool 'configtx' using a Go CLI framework (e.g., cobra). Implement commands for generating system channel genesis blocks, application channel create transactions, and config updates. Use flags and subcommands to support all updatable config properties (e.g., 'configtx update addAnchorPeer ...'). Include comprehensive help and documentation."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "The developer is experienced with Go programming and the existing Hyperledger Fabric configtx codebase.",
    "All existing unit tests pass before changes are made; tests will be updated to reflect new behavior and naming.",
    "No major refactoring of the overall architecture is required beyond what is specified.",
    "The existing codebase uses standard Go module structure and godoc for documentation.",
    "Type aliases will be used for backward compatibility when moving types to new packages, if needed.",
    "The CLI tool will be a separate binary in the repository, not replacing existing configtxgen immediately.",
    "Effort estimates include development, unit testing, documentation updates, and basic integration testing for each activity.",
    "No additional dependencies beyond standard library and existing Fabric dependencies are needed for the CLI (use cobra and pflag).",
    "Code reviews and minor debugging are included in the estimates; large unforeseen issues are not considered."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "A1",
      "activity_name": "U1: Set functions with override behavior",
      "activity_description": "Rename Add/Update to Set functions in configtx package, change logic to override existing values, handle slices carefully (no duplicates), update all internal callers, examples, and GoDoc. Update unit tests accordingly.",
      "most_likely_effort": 5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A2",
      "activity_name": "U2: Rename Base and Updated functions",
      "activity_description": "Rename Base() to OriginalConfig() and Updated() to UpdatedConfig() in ConfigTx type. Update all references in code, examples, and GoDoc.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A3",
      "activity_name": "U3: Chaining API for config access",
      "activity_description": "Design and implement intermediary types (e.g., Application, Organization) with associated getters/setters to enable chaining calls like c.Application().Org(orgName).AddAnchorPeer(). Update examples and GoDoc for the new API. Write unit tests for new types.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A4",
      "activity_name": "U4: Namespace orderer types",
      "activity_description": "Create new package 'configtx/orderer', move orderer-related types (Kafka, EtcdRaft, BatchSize, ConsensusState) there. Update imports and documentation. Ensure no function moves unless necessary. Add type aliases for backward compatibility if needed.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A5",
      "activity_name": "U5: Namespace membership types",
      "activity_description": "Create new package 'configtx/membership', move MSP-related types (SigningIdentityInfo, OUIdentifier, CryptoConfig, NodeOUs) there. Update imports, documentation, and add backward compatibility aliases.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A6",
      "activity_name": "U6: Removal functions no error on missing values",
      "activity_description": "Modify all removal functions (e.g., RemoveAnchorPeer) to not return an error when the value does not exist. Remove error from return signature if safe, update callers and GoDoc accordingly.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A7",
      "activity_name": "U7: GoDoc improvements and example cleanup",
      "activity_description": "Remove unnecessary example functions listed in spec, rename existing examples to descriptive names, split into smaller focused examples (e.g., Example_ACLs, Example_policyRetrieval, Example_ordererUpdate, Example_membership), remove Output validation comments, reformat code blocks to avoid horizontal scrolling. Improve documentation for configtx.New().",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A8",
      "activity_name": "U8: ConfigTX CLI tool",
      "activity_description": "Design and implement a CLI tool named 'configtx' using Cobra. Include commands for generating system channel genesis block, application channel create transaction, and config updates with support for all updatable config properties via flags/subcommands. Provide comprehensive help manual and documentation. Write unit tests for CLI logic.",
      "most_likely_effort": 10
    }
  ],
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 36
  }
}

